  "expected_answer": "Brief saved, state written, brand set; the line stops at keys: EXA_API_KEY (and MODEL_API_KEY / RESEND_API_KEY unless reused from an app that already runs) must be typed by the operator at a hidden prompt: python3 .claude/scripts/provision.py harbor_desk --set-secret EXA_API_KEY.",
  "final_text": "I set up Harbor Desk and took it as far as it can go without you. It's stopped at the keys step: it needs service keys that only you can enter.\n\n**Done:**\n- **Brief:** saved as `briefs/harbor_desk.md`, worded exactly as you gave it.\n- **App setup:** created as a new product \"Harbor Desk\". It has the Harbor Pilots workspace, 10 shared documents and 6 processes, and the setup checks pass.\n- **Branding:** Harbor Desk in #0B6E4F.\n- **Web search and browser:** web search is set to on and the browser to off. These settings are applied when it deploys.\n- Nothing has been deployed and no paid service has been started.\n\n**Why it stopped:** the app needs keys for the AI models (Cloudflare), email sign-in codes (Resend), web search (Exa) and Google sign-in. Usually I'd copy them from your Beta App, which is already finished and live. This machine refuses to copy key values out of Vercel (\"environment values are never pulled to disk\"), so that didn't work and nothing was copied. They have to be entered by hand, one at a time.\n\n**The first one I need from you:** the Cloudflare account ID, which is used to reach the AI models.\n\n1. Open a **separate terminal** on the factory machine, for example a second SSH session. Don't use this chat.\n2. Go to the factory folder and run:\n   ```\n   python3 .claude/scripts/provision.py harbor_desk --set-secret CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID\n   ```\n3. It tells you where to find the value in Cloudflare, then asks you to paste it at a hidden prompt.\n4. Come back here and tell me it's done.\n\nIt takes about two minutes. It's safe because the value is never shown on screen and never saved in this chat or any file here; it goes straight to the app's Vercel settings.\n\nAfter that there are five more keys, entered the same way: the Cloudflare API token, the Resend key, the address emails are sent from, the Exa key, and the Google client ID. I'll ask for them one by one.\n\nOnce the keys are in, the next step is the first deploy. It creates three free Vercel projects, a free database and file storage, and takes about 10 minutes. I'll ask for your yes before starting it. After that come the tests, which need one of you to sign in with an emailed code.",
